# The kernel's TLB maintenance seen from ring 3 (user/root/src/tlb.rs;
# docs/design.md, "TLB maintenance"). The root task maps a page read-write
# under its own page table, and a new page table with a page under it. A
# thread T in the root task's VSpace, alone at its priority while the root
# task waits on T's fault endpoint, loads a translation into the TLB with
# an access, changes the entry with an invocation, and accesses the page
# again: after Frame_Remap to read-only (invlpg), Frame_Unmap (invlpg) and
# PageTable_Unmap (a CR3 reload). Each second access must fault; a kernel
# that skips the flush lets it through a stale translation, T reports that,
# and the test fails. No other scenario sees a missing flush: test=vspace
# checks the entries by walking the tables. After each fault the root task
# undoes the change and replies, and the restarted access must find the
# page's word (from reviewer K's test=tlb: no other scenario restarts an
# access after a VMFault reply).
cmdline: test=tlb
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=tlb"
expect: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=tlb"
expect: tlb: page 0x500000 mapped read-write; a new page table maps page 0x600000
expect: tlb: ok   phase 1, Frame_Remap to read-only (invlpg): the access after it faulted at 0x500000
expect: fsr 0x7
expect: tlb: ok   phase 1: Frame_Remap read-write, then the fault reply: the access restarted and found 0xfffffffff814a112
expect: tlb: ok   phase 2, Frame_Unmap (invlpg): the access after it faulted at 0x500000
expect: fsr 0x4
expect: tlb: ok   phase 2: Frame_Map, then the fault reply: the access restarted and found 0xfffffffff814a112
expect: tlb: ok   phase 3, PageTable_Unmap (CR3 reload): the access after it faulted at 0x600000
expect: fsr 0x4
expect: tlb: ok   phase 3: PageTable_Map and Frame_Map, then the fault reply: the access restarted and found 0x7ab1e5eed
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
